WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:09.040
SPEAKER 1: BigQuery is a
fully managed data warehouse

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.300
that provides incredibly fast
SQL analytics over large data

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.300
sets.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.160
BigQuery provides
more than 100 data

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.320
sets publicly
available to analyze,

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.000
covering a variety
of data types,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.600
from historical weather to taxi
trips taken in New York City.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.480
We try to offer utility data
sets, such as the US census

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.420
data, so that customers can
join these data without needing

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.770
to import them.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.350
While these data sets are being
used in vital decision-making

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:33.940
across enterprises,
they are also

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:36.370
a great place to get
started with analyzing data

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.630
in BigQuery.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.260
Get started by navigating
to the Google Cloud console

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.570
at console.cloud.google.com.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:45.520
If you are new to Google
Cloud and BigQuery,

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.500
use the video linked in
the description below

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.050
to set up a new project
in the BigQuery sandbox.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.150
No credit card is required.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.980
Open the navigation window
and select Marketplace.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.685
In the left-hand menu, click
to filter by data sets.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:04.000
Each tile represents
a public data set.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.280
For example, the
American Community Survey

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.780
is an ongoing
survey that collects

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.110
social, economic, housing
and demographic data

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:14.990
by surveying more than 3 and 1/2
million US households annually.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:17.740
In addition to being used in
governmental funding decisions,

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.540
private businesses
also find this data

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.288
useful in their own
strategic decision-making.

00:01:22.288 --> 00:01:23.830
Clicking on the tile
will provide you

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.830
more detail on the
data set, including

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.770
a description of the data set,
sample queries, and metadata

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.180
showing information,
such as when

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:34.870
the data set was last updated,
and if there's a regular update

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:35.920
frequency.

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.920
To access the data set, click
the View Data Set button.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.890
This opens a new console
window and brings you

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:44.900
to the data set in
the BigQuery web UI.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.050
You can see each of the tables
available within the data set.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.470
In fact, you can scroll through
the other public data sets

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:53.730
in the program here as well.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.230
Back to the ACS data set.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.070
Click on a table, and you
will see the schema or columns

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.590
available in that table,
along with the table details,

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:04.680
including the size
and number of rows,

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.200
and a preview of the
first few rows of data.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.030
Click Query Table
and a template will

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.919
appear in the Query
Editor, which already

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:12.960
references the selected table.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.210
If you'd rather start with
one of the sample queries,

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.970
you can also click the Run this
Query button from the Details

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.960
page you were
looking at earlier.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:22.410
Let's look at this one.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.280
How has King County rent cost
as a share of median income

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:31.710
changed between 2011 and 2017?

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.165
In the Query Editor, click Run.

00:02:35.638 --> 00:02:37.430
And in just a few
seconds, you have a table

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.070
showing how the rent as a
percentage of median income

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:42.950
has changed for each
zip code in the county.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.500
Looking to analyze data
without writing SQL?

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:46.910
Just highlight
the table you wish

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:52.000
to analyze in the left-hand
nav, click Export,

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.700
and choose Explore in
Data Studio, Google's data

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.350
visualization tool.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.170
BigQuery charges for storage
and offers pay-as-you-go,

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:02.800
on-demand pricing or flat rate
pricing for predictability when

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.370
querying data.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.550
You can also take advantage
of the free tier option

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:08.090
to quickly get started.

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:11.890
Use the BigQuery sandbox to stay
safely within the free tier.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.590
More info on how to get started
in the BigQuery sandbox linked

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.563
in the description below.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.230
Happy analyzing.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.980
[MUSIC PLAYING]

